				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Backpack Lab: Filters Before Automation"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 9.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["28ED3EBB122D102D"]
			description: [
				"Begin with an Inventory Connector touching a small group of chests or barrels and attach a Storage Terminal where the network can see it. Confirm every container appears before extending the layout with cables."
				"A Crafting Terminal can request ingredients from connected storage, but recipe conflicts still belong to Polymorph or the recipe viewer. If an item disappears from the terminal, trace cables and connectors back to the core."
				"Keep the network inside reliably loaded base chunks, avoid circular or duplicate connections to the same inventory, and label physical storage anyway. Search is an interface, not a backup or an explanation of topology."
			]
			id: "2D0F242D77ABDD04"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2E5E90101E4A127F"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
